# Email Configuration

Controls which email account and inbox `/scan-email` reads from.
Strictly read-only — this plugin never marks emails as read, moves them,
or modifies them in any way.

---

## Settings

provider:     apple-mail
account_name: YOUR_MAIL_ACCOUNT_NAME
inbox_name:   INBOX

# Gmail (when provider: google) — see #65
# google_credentials_path: ~/.claude-eisenhower/google-client-secret.json
# google_token_path:       ~/.claude-eisenhower/google-gmail-refresh-token.json

---

## Providers

**apple-mail** (default, Mac-only) — wraps Apple Mail via `osascript`.
No auth required beyond the Mac's existing Mail account setup.

**google** — Gmail API over OAuth 2.0. Cross-platform.
Requires:
- `google_credentials_path` — abs path to the `client_secret.json` you
  download from Google Cloud Console. Gitignored. (May be the same
  client_secret file used by the Calendar adapter — see calendar-config.md.)
- `google_token_path` — abs path where the refresh token is persisted.
  Created automatically. Mode 0600. Gitignored.
- Scope: `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly`.

Issue tracker for the Gmail adapter: #65.

Note: as of foundation #67, the `/scan-email` command still drives
Apple Mail directly via embedded AppleScript. The dispatcher path
exists but is not yet wired up at the command surface — full
command rewire ships in a follow-up.

---

## How It's Used (apple-mail, today)

`/scan-email` reads `account_name` and `inbox_name` and drives Apple Mail
via inline AppleScript blocks:

```applescript
tell application "Mail"
  set targetAccount to first account whose name contains "{account_name}"
  set targetMailbox to mailbox "{inbox_name}" of targetAccount
end tell
```

## Settings Reference

**provider** — `apple-mail` (default) or `google`. Routing only; both
adapters return identical `EmailScanResult` shapes.

**account_name** — The name of the mail account in Apple Mail, or a unique
substring. Uses `contains` matching ("Acme" matches "Acme (you@acme.com)").
For Gmail provider, set to the full Gmail address.

**inbox_name** — Mailbox/label name. Common values:
- `INBOX` (Gmail default and most apple-mail accounts)
- `Inbox` (some accounts use title case)

To confirm the exact inbox name: run `/scan-email` and Claude will
auto-detect it in Step 2, or check Apple Mail → [Account] → inbox label.

## Scope Restriction

Only the configured account and inbox are ever read. No other mailboxes,
accounts, sent mail, or folders are accessed.

## How to Set Up

1. Copy this file: `cp email-config.md.example email-config.md`
2. Pick a provider:
   - **apple-mail** (Mac default): set `account_name` and `inbox_name`
     to the values from Apple Mail. Leave the `google_*` lines commented out.
   - **google**: blocked on #65 ship; foundation is in place.
3. The actual `email-config.md` is gitignored — never committed.
